<title>CROATIA: Croatia sells minority stake in automation firm.</title>
<headline>Croatia sells minority stake in automation firm.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatia's state privatisation agency on Monday sold its 0.17 percent stake in automation firm ATM d.d., the Zagreb Stock Exchange reported.</p>
<p>It said a package of 358 shares went to private brokerage Investco at 100 German marks each at a weekly discount auction for public debt bonds.</p>
<p>ATM is controlled by Croatian subsidiary of Germany's Siemens AG.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
